### 10. Common CDC Patterns for Exam

| Pattern | SQL/Code | When to Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Simple upsert** | `MERGE ... WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT` | SCD Type 1 batch |
| **Insert-only append** | `INSERT INTO target SELECT * FROM source WHERE NOT EXISTS (...)` | Append new records only |
| **SCD Type 2 MERGE** | UNION ALL trick with NULL merge_key (see section 4) | Batch history tracking |
| **Streaming SCD Type 2** | `dlt.apply_changes(stored_as_scd_type=2)` | SDP pipeline with history |
| **SQL streaming SCD** | `CREATE FLOW ... BY AUTO CDC ... STORED AS SCD TYPE 2` | DBSQL streaming CDC |
| **Incremental with CDF** | `spark.readStream.option('readChangeFeed', 'true').table(...)` | Downstream from Delta table |
| **Delete handling** | `WHEN MATCHED AND source.op = 'D' THEN DELETE` or `apply_as_deletes` | Propagate source deletes |
| **Dedup before merge** | `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY key ORDER BY ts DESC) = 1` | Multiple changes per key in one batch |

