### 11. Interview-Ready CDC Scenario

**"How did you implement real-time CDC from MySQL to Databricks?"**

| Step | Technology | Detail |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Capture | Debezium + Kafka Connect | Reads MySQL binlog, produces CDC events to Kafka |
| 2. Ingest | Auto Loader (cloudFiles) or Kafka source | Streams JSON CDC events into bronze streaming table |
| 3. Apply | `dlt.apply_changes()` in SDP | Deduplicates, orders by sequence, applies SCD Type 2 |
| 4. Enable downstream | Delta CDF on silver table | Gold layer reads only changes via `readChangeFeed` |
| 5. Serve | Materialized Views | Dashboards auto-refresh from gold aggregations |
| 6. Monitor | Expectations + row count reconciliation | `CONSTRAINT valid_key EXPECT (customer_id IS NOT NULL) ON VIOLATION DROP ROW` |

**Key metrics from production:**
- End-to-end latency: \~2 minutes (MySQL change → gold table)
- Volume: 500K CDC events/hour
- SCD Type 2 history table: 2 years, 800M rows
- Zero data loss: checkpointing + exactly-once semantics
